# Sprint Planning

## Overall Goal

This project is focusing on a major refactor of my existing "Gamenight" app that is currently terminal/CLI based. The refactor will turn the terminal-based app into a web app utilizing Flask. I will also include various tests utilizing `pytest`, `Selenium/Playwright`, and `pytest-bdd`. The goal is to make the app more user-friendly, more visually appealing, as well as implementing a few new features while integrating SQA practices learned in class to improve the quality and maintainability of the codebase.

## 1: Sprint Goals

#### Sprint 1 Goals (Set up):

- Establish base architecture for "GameNight" by creating a `GameService` layer and Flask app foundation from the CLI logic
- Adding minimal HTML UI for gameplay
- Writing basic pytests and integration tests for API and UI

#### Sprint 2 Goals (Validation, Persistent Scores, Leaderboard):

- Create server-side validation for game setup and moves
- Persist scores with SQL/SQLAlchemy
- Display a leaderboard on game selection screen

#### Sprint 3 Goals (UI Automation, BDD, Full Regression):

- Create `Selenium/Playwright` UI automation for core game flows
- Create BDD acceptance tests for "play game & see updated leaderboard"
- Clean up CI integration and regression practices

